<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    The other two stonecutting recipes (RimWorld: RecipeDefs/Recipes_Production ships one Make_Blocks_* per
    stone type). Recipes_Production.xml's own comment said its single sandstone recipe was "trimmed to one
    recipe until quarrying and chunk-yielding mining exist" — mining now yields chunks (Buildings_Natural.xml's
    mineableThing), so that blocker has expired and one recipe is a hole: ChunkGranite and ChunkLimestone came
    out of the ground and no recipe anywhere consumed either.

    Their own file rather than two more elements in Recipes_Production.xml, per CLAUDE.md: a new file cannot
    conflict with a lane editing the shared one, and DefLoader.AddDirectory loads both the same way.

    workAmount 1600 and 1 chunk -> 20 blocks, identical to Make_Blocks_Sandstone and to RimWorld, which prices
    every stone's cutting the same: the stone that is harder to cut is also the wall that lasts longer, and
    RimWorld puts the whole difference in the second half. No workSkill, matching RimWorld's stonecutting and
    the shipped sandstone recipe.

    Masonry, like the sandstone recipe and the bench itself (research.unlocks-content).
  -->

  <RecipeDef>
    <defName>Make_Blocks_Granite</defName>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>Masonry</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <label>cut granite blocks</label>
    <jobString>Cutting granite blocks.</jobString>
    <workAmount>1600</workAmount>
    <ingredients>
      <li>
        <filter><thingDefs><li>ChunkGranite</li></thingDefs></filter>
        <count>1</count>
      </li>
    </ingredients>
    <products><BlocksGranite>20</BlocksGranite></products>
    <recipeUsers><li>TableStonecutter</li></recipeUsers>
  </RecipeDef>

  <RecipeDef>
    <defName>Make_Blocks_Limestone</defName>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>Masonry</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <label>cut limestone blocks</label>
    <jobString>Cutting limestone blocks.</jobString>
    <workAmount>1600</workAmount>
    <ingredients>
      <li>
        <filter><thingDefs><li>ChunkLimestone</li></thingDefs></filter>
        <count>1</count>
      </li>
    </ingredients>
    <products><BlocksLimestone>20</BlocksLimestone></products>
    <recipeUsers><li>TableStonecutter</li></recipeUsers>
  </RecipeDef>

</Defs>
